  "example_summary": "Compute the tax liability for Mr. X with a total income of ₹ 16,00,000 under the default tax regime for A.Y.2026-27.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 115BAC Tax Slabs\n\n| Slab Range (Total Income) | Tax Rate (%) | Marginal Relief / Rebate Provisions |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Up to ₹ 4,00,000 | Nil | Initial basic exemption limit |\n| ₹ 4,00,001 to ₹ 8,00,000 | 5% | Tax calculated on incremental slab amount |\n| ₹ 8,00,001 to ₹ 12,00,000 | 10% | Tax calculated on incremental slab amount |\n| ₹ 12,00,001 to ₹ 16,00,000 | 15% | Tax calculated on incremental slab amount |\n| ₹ 16,00,001 to ₹ 20,000,000 | 20% | Tax calculated on incremental slab amount |\n| ₹ 20,000,001 to ₹ 24,00,000 | 25% | Tax calculated on incremental slab amount |\n| Above ₹ 24,00,000 | 30% | Highest marginal slab rate |\n\n\n### Core Statutory Rules\n\n* **Default Application:** The tax regime under Section 115BAC applies by default to all individual assessees unless expressly opted out where permissible.\n\n\n* **Cess Addition:** Health and Education Cess is levied at the mandatory rate of 4% on the computed income tax liability.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Surcharge Rate: Surcharge is applicable at varying percentage thresholds if total income exceeds specified statutory limits under Section 115BAC.",
